From 6248942054251a3903c8d712d2dd8fc5fe33f8a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:35:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/51] Size the subtitle background to the text (fit-content)
 and slim the horizontal padding

The background bar used to be a fixed-width container spanning nearly
the whole screen width, which looked grossly oversized for short cues.
It is now a fit-content block like an inline-block div around the text:

- Both layers wrap at the user-adjustable maximum width (no longer
  multiplied by the overall scale), then the bar is sized to the widest
  line actually used plus padding, hugging short cues tightly
- Both layers are re-laid out at that shared content width, so they
  stay perfectly centered inside the bar
- The padding setting now means the vertical padding (the gap between
  the text and the border above and below); the horizontal padding is
  half of it, because the bar hugs the text closely on the left and
  right
- The outline width of the no-background mode follows each layer's
  actual (auto-shrunk) font size
